<codeline><highlight class="normal">###<sp/>Findings</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">The<sp/>FFT<sp/>soft-max<sp/>implementation<sp/>achieves<sp/>a<sp/>substantial<sp/>computational<sp/>speedup<sp/>for<sp/>large<sp/>radii,<sp/>reaching<sp/>up<sp/>to<sp/>$10.74\times$<sp/>faster<sp/>than<sp/>direct<sp/>GPU<sp/>expansion<sp/>at<sp/>radius<sp/>128<sp/>on<sp/>$512\times512$.<sp/>Direct<sp/>spatial<sp/>expansion<sp/>scales<sp/>non-linearly<sp/>with<sp/>radius<sp/>because<sp/>morphological<sp/>operations<sp/>are<sp/>generally<sp/>non-separable<sp/>in<sp/>2D.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">However,<sp/>the<sp/>soft-max<sp/>approximation<sp/>introduces<sp/>major<sp/>quality<sp/>deficiencies:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">-<sp/>The<sp/>smooth<sp/>exponential<sp/>soft-max<sp/>does<sp/>not<sp/>reproduce<sp/>the<sp/>sharp<sp/>plateau<sp/>and<sp/>boundary<sp/>characteristics<sp/>of<sp/>an<sp/>exact<sp/>morphological<sp/>dilation.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">-<sp/>Tuning<sp/>the<sp/>sharpness<sp/>parameter<sp/>$\beta$<sp/>leads<sp/>to<sp/>numerical<sp/>overflow<sp/>or<sp/>underflow<sp/>issues<sp/>in<sp/>floating-point<sp/>ranges<sp/>without<sp/>fully<sp/>matching<sp/>the<sp/>discrete<sp/>maximum.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">-<sp/>For<sp/>small<sp/>and<sp/>moderate<sp/>radii,<sp/>the<sp/>constant<sp/>overhead<sp/>of<sp/>FFT<sp/>transforms<sp/>outweighs<sp/>any<sp/>scaling<sp/>benefit.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">Conclusion:<sp/>FFT<sp/>soft-max<sp/>expansion<sp/>is<sp/>computationally<sp/>faster<sp/>for<sp/>very<sp/>large<sp/>radii,<sp/>but<sp/>the<sp/>loss<sp/>of<sp/>output<sp/>accuracy<sp/>and<sp/>fidelity<sp/>makes<sp/>it<sp/>unsuitable<sp/>as<sp/>a<sp/>replacement<sp/>for<sp/>morphological<sp/>operations.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">##<sp/>4.<sp/>Overall<sp/>Decision</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">Neither<sp/>FFT<sp/>approach<sp/>is<sp/>adopted<sp/>into<sp/>the<sp/>production<sp/>pipeline:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">-<sp/>**Convolution**:<sp/>Retain<sp/>the<sp/>GPU<sp/>separable<sp/>implementation<sp/>(`smooth_cpulse`).</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">-<sp/>**Morphological<sp/>Expansion**:<sp/>Retain<sp/>the<sp/>GPU<sp/>spatial<sp/>implementation<sp/>(`expand`).</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">Re-evaluating<sp/>FFT-based<sp/>approximations<sp/>would<sp/>only<sp/>be<sp/>justified<sp/>if<sp/>an<sp/>alternative<sp/>formulation<sp/>eliminates<sp/>soft-max<sp/>approximation<sp/>error<sp/>without<sp/>sacrificing<sp/>execution<sp/>speed.</highlight></codeline>
